          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: आदर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आदर (ādar) — \"respect\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit ādara, 'regard, attentiveness', from ā-dṛ-, 'to heed'. Hindi carries this word inside its own machinery: the आप form is called ādar-sūcak, the respect-marking form."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So this is not only a word for a feeling somebody has. It is the name of a choice the language makes you make in nearly every sentence you speak, whether you have thought about it or not."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three, and this one is built into the grammar."
            }
          ]
        },
