        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: प्रणाम",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्रणाम (praṇām) — \"a bow, a salutation\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit pra-ṇāma, 'a bending forward', on nam-, 'to bow' — the identical root standing inside नमस्ते and नमस्कार. Three words, one gesture, three heights of formality."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्रणाम (praṇām) is what a younger person says to an elder, often while bending to touch the feet, and what it expects back is आशीर्वाद (āśīrvād). The pair of words is the pair of movements: one goes down, one comes back over the top."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and the run is closed: gratitude, a favour, respect, a blessing, a bow."
            }
          ]
        },
